  "unknowns": [
    "V4.1 is the supplied file revision; the schematic title-block revision and physical PCB revision are unconfirmed. Actual fitting and jumper positions were not inspected.",
    "W25Q128 heading and 64 Mbit symbol note conflict. Explicit NOR fitting permits its SPI transport only; the exact expected JEDEC identity and geometry require separate reviewed device configuration.",
    "MAX485 and MAX232 symbols show 3.3 V supply although those standard part names specify 5 V supply. Verify actual compatible part markings and electrical conditions before physical use.",
    "P21 selects USB FS or CAN1 on PA11/PA12; P15 selects RS485 or CAN2-related connections. Authored hardware selections are declarations, not inspection evidence.",
    "Ethernet MDIO PA2 conflicts with the default USART2 RS485 TX route; original wiring cannot deliver both simultaneously.",
    "DP83848 Y3 frequency is unspecified; P5 MDIO labels differ between sheets. PHY address, reference clock, RX_DV wiring compatibility and continuity require review. No V4.1 Ethernet binding is admitted yet.",
    "PF6/PF7/PF8/PF9 directional keys lack drawn external pullups; select input and explicit internal pullup. The fifth center key is NRST, not another GPIO.",
    "Touch uses mixed PA5/PB1/PB2 GPIO, not a complete hardware SPI route. Audio control PC0/PC13 and camera control PD6/PD7 are not hardware I2C routes.",
    "USB_HS on PB14/PB15 uses an internal FS PHY path without ULPI; no 480 Mbps or USB host support is implied.",
    "FSMC SRAM/LCD, SDIO, RTC, full audio and DCMI drivers remain separate implementation tasks, not support established by this Board package.",
    "ILI9341/XPT2046 module identities are user-declared; actual connector continuity and fitting remain unverified. Display/touch options do not imply a delivered FSMC or complete device driver. GPIO touch PEN and EXTI PEN are alternative owners and cannot both be selected.",
    "Camera, WM8978/VS1053, WiFi/Bluetooth, DS18B20 and HS0038 module variants and fitting remain unverified.",
    "FSMC NE3 is an explicitly declared IS62WV51216 1MiB reference. Exact fitted speed/voltage suffix, encoded bank timing and physical waveform need verification; no memory test or DMA reachability follows from a CPU window.",
    "Audio and camera choices currently select reviewed GPIO control wires only; they neither select a codec/sensor automatically nor establish I2S/DCMI software support or fitting. DS18B20 external VDD and HS0038/NEC are explicit software references, with no inferred remote model or parasite power support."
  ],
